{
 "sub_strand": "MATH.G7.GEOMET.ANGLES",
 "title": "Angles",
 "status": "draft: written 17 Nov 2026 offline for the Grade 7 pilot; not yet checked by a Kenyan maths teacher; not loaded by the live tutor",
 "sources": [],
 "notes": "Official outcomes a to g are tested; h is an attitude. Angles on a straight line add to 180 and vertically opposite angles are equal (a); angles at a point add to 360 (b); alternate and corresponding angles are equal and co-interior angles add to 180 (c); in a parallelogram opposite angles are equal and neighbouring angles add to 180 (d); angle properties of triangles and quadrilaterals, and the angle sum of a polygon from the triangles it splits into, (n - 2) x 180 (e, f); exterior angles add to 360 and an interior and exterior angle at a corner add to 180 (f); angles and sides of regular polygons up to the hexagon (g). Grade 6 found angles on a straight line and the angle sum of triangles and rectangles. The older families were filed under letters from an earlier draft; the parallelogram families are filed under d and the triangle and quadrilateral families under e.",
 "skills": [
  {
   "skill": "MATH.G7.GEOMET.ANGLES.ANGLES_ON_LINE",
   "key_step": "The child writes the angles on a line equal to 180, solves for x, and puts x back.",
